-- title:
--   Frobenius rebasing of a rigidification: Xi moves by Zᶜ
-- statement:
--   The setting is the one in which the Čerednik–Drinfeld dictionary for fake elliptic curves is set up, and all of its data enter as hypotheses.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** Primes $r$, $\bar r$ and a nonzero level $N$, with $\bar r \neq r$, $r \nmid N$, $\bar r \nmid N$ and $N$ squarefree. A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible $\pi \in \mathcal O$, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, with residue ring of cardinality $r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$ (absolute ramification one), together with a characteristic-zero fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$. An $\mathcal O$-algebra $\mathrm{Onr}$ which is a characteristic-zero domain, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $\mathrm{Onr}$ is complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $\mathrm{Onr}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo it (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $\mathrm{Onr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo it (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r}$ modulo it (`hFr`): $\mathrm{Onr}$ is the completion of the maximal unramified extension with its Frobenius. A monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ which, by `hvdet`, sends $g$ to $n$ exactly when $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some $u \in \mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   **The indefinite side and its moduli.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB` asserting that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite ($0<a$ or $0<b$) and that its completion at a finite place is a division algebra precisely at the places above $r$ and $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$. A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a point assignment $\mathrm{pt}$ which, by `h𝒳`, is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and $N$-level structure. A full level $n \ge 3$ with $r \nmid n$, $\bar r \nmid n$, $\gcd(n,N)=1$; a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with $\mathrm{ptF}$ a fine moduli space for curves with full level $n$ (`hM`), a group $G$ acting by automorphisms $\rho$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ realising the level twists (`hρ`), and a morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ which is $G$-invariant and forgets the full level on points (`hp`, `hρp`, `hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, a coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ for curves with an extra level-$\ell$ structure (`h𝒴`), with degeneracy maps $d_0,d_1 : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ which on points forget the extra level, respectively pass to an $\ell$-isogenous quotient (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`, `hd₀`, `hd₁`). Atkin–Lehner morphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r} : \mathcal X \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ inducing the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`harf`, `harbarf`, `har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The definite side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef` asserting $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is a division algebra exactly at the places above $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$, an idele $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ such that $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`), an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$, and the place $v$ above $r$. The subgroup $\Gamma_t$ is characterised by `hΓt` as the group of units integral away from $v$; elements $s_\ell$, $s_{f,\ell}$ for each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ satisfy `hs`: $s_{f,\ell}$ has component $s_\ell$ at every place not above $r$ and trivial component above $r$, the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $s_{f,\ell}^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $(\Lambda_1, \mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1)$ at $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$; $\Gamma_{t,\ell}$ is $\Gamma_t$ intersected with its conjugate by $s_\ell$ (`hΓtℓ`); and $\bar w$ has reduced norm $\bar r$ and normalises $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **The base point and the endomorphism dictionary.** The hypothesis `hΛℤ` places all rational integers in $\Lambda$, and `hcoord` makes $\mathrm{coord}$ an order coordinate for $\Lambda$ at $r$. Over the residue ring $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$ there are a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of length two along the unit section with `hA₀` asserting that $A_0$ is a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$, and families $e, e' : \Gamma_t \to \mathrm{End}(A_0)$ with degrees $\deg$. The clauses `hE1` (each $(e\gamma, e'\gamma)$ an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the $N$-level), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity of $e$ up to multiplication by powers of $r$), `hE1sc` (rational scalars $\gamma = c$ go to multiplication by $c$ up to powers of $r$), `hE1'` (conversely, if $e\gamma$ is a multiplication up to a power of $r$ then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar), `hE2` (for every injective ring homomorphism of the centraliser of the $\mathbb Z_{r^2}$-action and of $\varpi$ on $X_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is a single conjugator $g$ matching, for each $\gamma$, an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser which induces $e\gamma$ on the formal coordinates, with image $r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), `hE3` (labelling of the $\Gamma_t$-action on full level-$n$ structures by elements of $\Lambda$, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$), `hE4` (every $r$-power-degree level-preserving isogeny pair on a fake elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field pulled back from $A_0$ is, up to powers of $r$, induced by some $e\gamma$), together with the order $R_2 \le R_1$ capturing $R_1$ up to $r$-power denominators, the endomorphisms $\hat e$ of $A_0$ attached to $R_2$ and the clauses `hE5a`, `hE5b1`–`hE5b3`, `hE5c`, `hE5d`, `hE5e` (additivity, $\Lambda$-equivariance and level preservation of $\hat e$; $\hat e(1) = \mathrm{id}$; anti-multiplicativity; $\hat e$ of an integer is multiplication by it; $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x)$ is multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$; compatibility of $\hat e$ with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma_t$; and a joint matrix dictionary for $\Gamma_t$ and $R_2$ with one common conjugator) are all assumed.
--
--   **The formal-module side.** A ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathbb Z_{r^2} \to \mathrm{Onr}$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $\mathrm{MD}$ over $\mathrm{Onr}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), a classifying map $\eta$ from rigidified objects, and `hη` in three clauses: $\eta$ separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, commutes with base change along ring maps over $\mathrm{Onr}$, and every section of $\mathrm{MD}$ is, on a finite cover by localisations generating the unit ideal, of the form $\eta$ of an admissible rigidified object. An injective homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi_\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is sandwiched between the matrices over $\mathcal O$ by a single power of $r$ (`hE₀`).
--
--   **Drinfeld's comparison.** A family of maps $e_D$ from the points of $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.G}\,\mathcal O\,\mathrm{MD}$ to pairs consisting of an $\mathrm{Onr}$-leg and a Deligne datum over $K_0,\pi$, natural in $\mathcal O$-algebra maps (`hnatD`), bijective on every Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra (`hbijD`), compatible with the legs (`hfstD`), transporting the relation `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy` into the twisted $\mathrm{GL}_2$-action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` for $\pi$, $\mathrm{Onr}$, $\mathrm{Fr}$, $\mathrm{vdet}$ (`hGLD`), transporting $\varpi$-translation into the one-step Frobenius twist of the leg with unchanged datum (`hPiD`), and with $\varpi$-translates always existing (`hPiexD`).
--
--   **Comparison of the two formal modules.** A ring homomorphism $\kappa : \mathrm{Onr}/(\pi) \to \mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ compatible with the two quotient maps (`hκ`), an integer $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which by `hβ₀` is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ pushed along $\kappa$. A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$.
--
--   **The Atkin–Lehner partner of the base point.** A fake elliptic curve $A_{0w}$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$ with morphisms $a_w$, $a_w'$ realising the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ from $A_0$ (`hALw`), an $r$-power isogeny pair $(b_w,b_w')$ from $A_{0w}$ back to $A_0$ of degree $r^{k_w}$ preserving the level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw`, which adds to the dictionary of `hE2`, with the same conjugator, an element $\varepsilon_w$ of the centraliser inducing $a_w \ggg b_w$ on the formal coordinates and with matrix $r^{k_w}\,g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$.
--
--   **The supersingular dictionary.** A map $\Xi$ sending, for every Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ and $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to B$, a rigidified fake elliptic curve over $(B,\psi)$ to a point of $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.G}\,\mathcal O\,\mathrm{MD}$ over $B$, subject to: `hΞleg`, the leg of $\Xi$ of a rigidified curve over a connected $B$ is an integral Frobenius twist of $\psi$; `hΞnat`, compatibility with pullback of rigidified curves along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps; `hΞiso`, invariance of $\Xi$ under isomorphisms of the underlying curve that can be matched on the reductions and on the auxiliary pullbacks of $A_0$ up to powers of $r$; and `hΞdef`, which over a connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent computes $\Xi$ explicitly: for every rigidified curve whose underlying curve is a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$ with data $(X,\theta)$ there are $j \le 1$ and a rigidified object $t$ over $B$ with $t.X = X$, which is a rigidification transport of $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$ at level $j$, admissible for the leg $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$, and $\Xi$ of the curve is the triple consisting of that leg, the nilpotence of $r$, and $\eta$ of $t$. Finally a matrix $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and two equivariance clauses: `heqΓ`, that a translation of a rigidification by $e\gamma$ is implemented on $\Xi$ by the action of $Z^{c} g_0 \iota_0(\gamma) g_0^{-1}$ for some $c \in \mathbb Z$, where $Z$ is the central unit of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ given by the scalar $r$; and `heqW`, the analogous clause for an Atkin–Lehner-at-$\bar r$ quotient of the curve (with $\bar r$ invertible on $B$) matched on the rigidifications through $a_w \ggg b_w$, implemented by the action of $Z^{c} g_0 \iota_0(\bar w) g_0^{-1}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ becomes nilpotent and whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to B$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ with $\Lambda$-action and $N$-level, every rigidification $\rho$ of $E$ relative to $A_0$ and the leg $\psi$ (that is: a reduction $\rho.E_b$ of $E$ modulo $\pi$, a pullback $\rho.A_b$ of $A_0$ along the residue leg, and an isogeny pair $\rho.\varphi$, $\rho.\varphi'$ of degree $r^{\rho.d}$ between them preserving the level), every $k \in \mathbb Z$ and every $\psi'$ with $\psi' = \psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{k}$, there exist a rigidification $\rho'$ of the *same* curve $E$ relative to the leg $\psi'$ and an integer $c$ such that the following three assertions hold.
--
--   First, $\Xi(E,\rho)$ and $\Xi(E,\rho')$ are related by the action of the central element $Z^{c}$, in the sense of `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy` for $\iota, \Phi, \eta, \mathrm{Fr}, E_0$: there are an element $\varepsilon$ of the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and of $\varpi_\Phi$ and naturals $k', m'$ with $E_0\varepsilon = r^{k'} (Z^{c})^{-1}$, with kernel of degree $r^{2m'}$, such that the leg of $\Xi(E,\rho')$ is the $(m'-2k')$-fold Frobenius twist of that of $\Xi(E,\rho)$ and the two underlying sections of $\mathrm{MD}$ lift, Zariski-locally on $B$, to admissible rigidified objects related by translation by $\varepsilon$.
--
--   Second, for every prime $\ell \neq r$ invertible in $B$, every extra level-$\ell$ structure on $A_0$ (the Lean binder for it reuses the name `K₀`) and every pair $C$, $C'$ of extra level-$\ell$ structures on $E$: if $C$ is transported from that structure through $\rho$, meaning that for every scheme $T$, every morphism $t'$ from $T$ to the spectrum of $B/(\pi)$ and every $T$-point $R$ of $\rho.E_b$ over $t'$, whenever $R$ followed by $\rho.g_b$ factors through the level subscheme of $C$ then $R$ followed by $\rho.\varphi$ and then $\rho.g_A$ factors through the level subscheme of the structure on $A_0$, and if $C'$ is transported from the same structure through $\rho'$ in the same sense, then $C$ and $C'$ have the same points: for every scheme $T$, every $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} B$ and every $T$-point $R$ of $E$ over $t$, $R$ factors through the level subscheme of $C$ if and only if it factors through that of $C'$.
--
--   Third, for all full level-$n$ structures $P_n$, $P_n'$ on $E$, if $P_n$ is a norm-level transport of $P_0$ along $\rho$ and $P_n'$ is one along $\rho'$ (in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.IsNormLevelTransport` for $\mathrm{Fr}, \theta_0, \kappa, \beta_0, \Phi, \iota, \mathrm{coord}$), then multiplication of $P_n'$ by $r^{\max(c,0)}$ and multiplication of $P_n$ by $r^{\max(-c,0)}$ agree as sections of $E$ over $\operatorname{Spec} B$; that is, the two height-normalised transported full level structures differ by the $r$-power $r^{c}$.
--
--   This is the $\mathbb Z$-fold iterate of the one-step Frobenius rebasing in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison: changing the unramified leg $\psi$ of a rigidified fake elliptic curve by an arbitrary integral power of Frobenius can be absorbed by a new rigidification of the same curve, at the cost of the central action of a power of $r$ on the Drinfeld side, while the transported prime-to-$r$ extra level structures are unchanged and the height-normalised transported full level-$n$ structures differ by that same power of $r$. It is used in the construction of an even (Frobenius-parity-normalised) rigidification in [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_even_rigidification_of_isActBy_of_isPiTranslate_normLevel_rpow`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_even_rigidification_of_isActBy_of_isPiTranslate_normLevel_rpow), and through it in the $p$-adic uniformisation of the Shimura curve at $r$.
